journal.pmed.0040309</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mbogo</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Mwangangi</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nzovu</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gu</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Yan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gunter</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name><name><surname>Swalm</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Keating</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Regens</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Shililu</surname><given-names>JI</given-names></name><name><surname>Githure</surname><given-names>JI</given-names></name><name><surname>Beier</surname><given-names>JC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Spatial and temporal heterogeneity of Anopheles mosquitoes and <italic>Plasmodium falciparum </italic>transmission along the Kenyan coast</article-title><source>Am J Trop Med Hyg</source><year>2003</year><volume>68</volume><fpage>734</fpage><lpage>742</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12887036</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Onori</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Payne</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Grab</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Grab</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Horst</surname><given-names>HI</given-names></name><name><surname>Almeida</surname><given-names>FJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Joia</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Incipient resistance of <italic>Plasmodium falciparum </italic>to chloroquine among a semi-immune population of the United Republic of Tanzania. 1